    "text": "To determine the cost of an annual newspaper subscription with a 20% discount, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total cost of a monthly subscription for a year.\n2. Apply the 20% discount to the total monthly cost.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total cost of a monthly subscription for a year.\nThe cost of a monthly subscription is $10. Since there are 12 months in a year, the total cost for a year is:\n\\[ 10 \\times 12 = 120 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nStep 2: Apply the 20% discount to the total monthly cost.\nA 20% discount means you pay 80% of the total monthly cost. So, we calculate 80% of $120:\n\\[ 120 \\times 0.80 = 96 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nTherefore, the final amount you end up paying for the annual subscription is:\n\\[ \\boxed{96} \\]",
